---
title: Best Vegetarian Lasagna
image: https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/vegetarian-lasagna-500x500.jpg
prep time: 40 minutes
source: https://www.loveandlemons.com/vegetarian-lasagna
cook time: 50 minutes
author: Jeanine Donofrio, Phoebe Moore
cuisine: American, Italian
time required: 1 hour 30 minutes
servings: 8
tags: main-dish, time-intensive
course: Main dish
---

Preheat the oven to 425°F and line a #baking sheet{} with parchment paper. Oil a 9x13-inch baking dish with @extra-virgin olive oil{}.

Place @cremini mushrooms{8%ounces}(stemmed and quartered), @red bell pepper{1}(stemmed, seeded, and cut into 1-inch pieces), @zucchini{1 medium}(cut into ½-inch pieces), and @yellow onion{½ medium}(cut into ½-inch pieces) on the baking sheet. Drizzle with @extra-virgin olive oil{}, sprinkle with @sea salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{}, and toss to coat. Spread evenly on the baking sheet and roast for ~{20-25%minutes}, or until tender and browned around the edges. Reduce the oven temperature to 400°F.

Meanwhile, cook the @lasagna noodles{15}. Bring a large #pot{} of salted water to a boil and prepare the lasagna noodles according to the package instructions, cooking until al dente. Drain and toss with a drizzle of @extra-virgin olive oil{} to prevent sticking.

Make the ricotta filling: In a large bowl, stir together @whole milk ricotta cheese{3 cups}(24 ounces), @garlic{3%cloves}(grated), @lemon zest{2%teaspoons}, @sea salt{=1%tsp}, and several grinds of @freshly ground black pepper{}.

== Assembly ==

Spread @marinara sauce{3 cups}(24 ounces) at the bottom of the prepared baking dish. Top with a layer of @lasagna noodles{}, followed by half the ricotta mixture. Spread the ricotta in an even layer, then arrange half the @fresh spinach{} evenly on top. Top with half the roasted vegetables and dot with ⅔ cup of the remaining @marinara sauce{}.

Repeat with another layer of @lasagna noodles{}, followed by the remaining ricotta, @fresh spinach{}, roasted vegetables, and another ⅔ cup of @marinara sauce{}. Top with the remaining @lasagna noodles{}.

Spread the remaining ⅔ cup of @marinara sauce{} over the pasta, then evenly sprinkle with @grated low-moisture, part-skim mozzarella cheese{2 cups} and @grated pecorino cheese{½ cup}. Bake in the 400°F oven for ~{30%minutes}, or until the cheese is browned and bubbling. Let stand for ~{20%minutes} before garnishing with @fresh basil leaves{} or @chopped fresh parsley{} (for garnish), slicing, and serving.